# {{crate_name}}

F Prime sequences for this deployment, compiled to WebAssembly and run on board by
[`Svc::WasmSequencer`](https://github.com/nasa/fprime).

## Building

```shell
rustup target add {{target}}
cargo build --release
```

## Adding a sequence

```shell
fprime-wasm add <name>
```

This writes `src/bin/<name>.rs` and hooks it into the `cargo` build system.

## Building sequences

```shell
cargo build --release
```

Builds final `.wasm` binaries to `target/{{target}}/release/*.wasm`.
These binaries can be uplinked and executed on-board using the WasmSequencer.

## Verifying a sequence

```shell
fprime-wasm verify
```

Dry-run each module with the on-board Wasm interpreter to collect memory usage metrics.
Memory-usage metrics are validated against the `sequencer.toml` limits to make sure the
configured settings on-board _can_ execute the module.

### Limits

`sequencer.toml` holds the default set of memory settings of the WasmSequencer. These
settings may be tuned to match your project's setting. Note that some of these settings
are mapped to per-sequencer-instance settings and therefore multiple `.toml` files may
be needed to model each instance.

## Dictionary

`{{dictionary}}` is this deployment's dictionary, and `build.rs` turns it into the
typed API the sequences call. Replace it from a newer release build and re-run
`cargo build --release`.
